## Key Entities

### Data Types Cached

| Entity Type | Database Table | Cache Key Format | TTL | Use Case |
|-------------|----------------|------------------|------|----------|
| `FoodItem` | food_item | `weekly_menu.food_details:{item_id}` | 30m | Display food info in menus |
| `MenuItem` | menu_items | `order.menu_items:{order_id}:{menu_item_id}` | 15m | Show order contents |
| `OrderItem` | order_line_items | `catering_menu.items:{catering_id}` | 60m | Catering lookup |
| `Category` | food_category | `food_catalog.categories:{cat_id}` | 24h | Filter/sort menu items |

### Cache Key Examples

```
tenant_a:weekly_menu.food_details:123     # Item 123 from tenant A's weekly menu
tenant_b:order.menu_items:987              # Menu items for order 987 (tenant B)
tenant_a:catering_menu.items:555           # Catering items for catering order 555
```

### Cache Entry Structure (eko/gocache memory store format)

```go
type CacheEntry[K comparable, V any] struct {
    Key      K                    // Cache key (includes tenant prefix)
    Value    V                    // Actual data value
    TTL      time.Duration        // Time-to-live duration
    Created  time.Time            // When entry was created/stored
    Expired  bool                 // Whether this should be evicted
}

// eko/gocache stores these in a map[K]CacheEntry[V] internally (sync.Map)
```

